Hypothesis (gap_norm_rmsnorm): Replacing LayerNorm with RMSNorm in the pre-norm 4-layer character-level Transformer, with the fixed 2,000-step budget unchanged, will leave validation cross-entropy unchanged within seed-to-seed noise.
Mechanism: The retrieved claims describe Pre-LN Transformers as substitutable by Pre-RMSNorm counterparts at almost no cost, offering the same arithmetic functionality. Their stated gain is training and inference time, i.e. computational efficiency. The path's efficiency-to-quality links (x2004_05150_1, x2609_07264_1) concern compute-matched comparisons. Here the budget is a fixed number of steps, not a fixed wall-clock or compute budget, so faster steps do not buy extra optimization. Any efficiency benefit should therefore not show up as lower validation loss.
Predicted direction: no_change
Falsification: The hypothesis is contradicted if the paired per-seed delta in validation cross-entropy (RMSNorm minus LayerNorm) is consistently on one side of zero, in either direction, by more than the baseline's measured seed-to-seed noise.

